/AP << /N 5840 0 R >> /Contents (Read Transaction:\012\012A read uses 2 channels\012AR Channel: Read address/control\012R Channel: Read data + Read response\012\012Flow: \012Master sends read address to slave\012Slae sends read data back to master\012\012Write Transaction:\012\012AW Channel: Write address/control\012W chanel: Write data\012B Channel: Write response\012\012Flow:\012Master sends write address to slave.\012Master sends write data to slave\012Slave sends write response back to master\012\012Because for a read, the response comes back together with the read data on the R channel.\012\012For a write, the data only goes from master to the slave, so the slave still needs a separate way to say: I received the write and it completed successfully or failed\012)
